;;; A macro's call inside a fact a `(solve … :expect (region …))` claim lists loads, and the claim
;;; can never hold —
;;; M1f **W86**, register row `W86/macro-call-in-region-claim`, filed by S1f.7.12 (T1f.7.12.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, a macro `settled`, the fact `(says (paid Ann))`, and a region claim whose model
;;; lists `(says (settled Ann))`. No candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A region claim lists a state's stored facts, and a fact is not expanded: no state holds the
;;; listed one. Refused at load, at the call, one line, on every command.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `91b12be8`, release: the program loads; R is {∅}, and the claim is FAILED, *the model
;;; lists (says (settled Ann)), which the state does not hold*: `ein solve` exits 1, every other
;;; command 0.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.12 (T1f.7.12.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(relation says Claim :why "it is said that {?1}")
(macro settled (?g) (paid ?g) :why "{?g} has settled: they have paid")
(says (paid Ann))
(solve :hypothesis-relations () :expect (region (model (says (settled Ann)))))
